     "<div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\">rmr 1.3 offers:</span></font></div><ul style=\"margin:15px 0px;padding:0px 0px 0px 30px;border:0px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;font-size:13.63636302947998px;line-height:20px\"><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">An optional vectorized API for efficient R programming when dealing with small records.</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Fast C implementations for serialization and deserialization from and to typedbytes.</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Other readers and writers work much better in vectorized mode, namely csv and text</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Additional steps to support structured data better, that is you can use more data frames and less lists in the API</li><li style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">More forgiving behavior for package loading and bug fixes</li></ul><ul style=\"margin:15px 0px;padding:0px 0px 0px 30px;border:0px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;font-size:13.63636302947998px;line-height:20px\"><li>More details here: <a href=\"http://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/4efbd435aff3d52cfea116b663100baf637035cc/rmr/pkg/docs/new-in-this-release.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/4efbd435aff3d52cfea116b663100baf637035cc/rmr/pkg/docs/new-in-this-release.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792493184350000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZQAbVeAg8n8yyNRxj0RUA\">New in this release</a><br></li><li>Code speaks: <a href=\"https://github.com/downloads/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/rmr_1.3.tar.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/downloads/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/rmr_1.3.tar.gz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792493184350000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00rR6E2QOy6Q2y0hB279rU\">rmr_1.3.tar.gz</a><br></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/master/rmr/pkg/docs/introduction-to-vectorized-API.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/master/rmr/pkg/docs/introduction-to-vectorized-API.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792493184350000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3i2_mXMESAoElqUFK-3-_7\">Introduction to the vectorized API</a><br></li></ul><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\">We&#39;ve made an effort to upgrade and reorganize the documentation around a new process whereby code-heavy documentation is versioned and tested just like the library itself, thanks to RStudio and knitr, but this process will be complete with the next minor. Enjoy and don&#39;t hold back your feedback.</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica, arial, freesans, clean, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:16.66666603088379px\">Antonio</span></font></div>"
